    "title": "Feel the love: Belmont becomes a Purple Heart Community - NewsBreak",
    "text": "laconiadailysun.com\nwebsite\nBelmont\nFeel the love: Belmont becomes a Purple Heart Community\nBy Katlyn Proctor,\n10 hours agoThe Town of Belmont officially became a Purple Heart Community on Wednesday, just in time for National Purple Heart Day on Aug. 7. Two Belmont residents who received the Purple Heart medal — John Monahan and Stephen Craig Santi — were remembered for their wartime service as an official proclamation was read by Selectboard Chair Ruth Mooney. Cemetery Trustee Hillary Horn is responsible for organizing the designation, which will feature four road signs throughout Belmont, welcoming visitors to town. Belmont is the 22nd municipality in New Hampshire to become a Purple Heart Community, designated by the Military Order of the Purple Heart.",
